            "image_size": 0,
            "border_text": "",
            "title": "DIY Clay Footprint:",
            "subtitle": "",
            "text": "<p>We wanted to share the sweetest little DIY keepsake idea with you. A beautiful footprint of your baby’s foot to treasure and keep for years to come. Perhaps for yourself or maybe as the perfect gift for baby’s grandparents 🤎 Follow the easy steps below and capture a small but special moment in your baby’s life.</p>",
            "text2": "",
            "content_width": 450,
            "content_width_image": 450,
            "center": false,
            "fill_height": true,
            "mirror": true,
            "section_background": "",
            "content_background": "",
            "content_text": "",
            "content_accent": "",
            "width": "default",
            "margin": 5,
            "section_padding": 0,
            "padding": 0
          }
        },
        "3f7cd7c2-010b-4b9a-afc8-8d91f287bf4611": {
          "type": "article_2",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image004.jpg",
            "image_size": 0,
            "border_text": "",
            "title": "Step 1:",
            "subtitle": "",
            "text": "<p>Find all the materials needed:</p>",
            "text2": "<ul>\n<li>A clean dust free surface to work on</li>\n<li>A Packet of non-toxic Air-drying clay</li>\n<li>A rolling pin</li>\n<li>Letter stamps</li>\n<li>Natural string</li>\n<li>A felt pen, in the colors of your choice.</li>\n<li>A chopstick or straw to create the hole</li>\n</ul>",
            "content_width": 450,
            "content_width_image": 450,
            "center": false,
            "fill_height": true,
            "mirror": false,
            "section_background": "",
            "content_background": "",
            "content_text": "",
            "content_accent": "#d99940",
            "width": "default",
            "margin": 5,
            "section_padding": 0,
            "padding": 0
          }
        },
        "d6991ca0-9d51-446c-8d85-6727e9164d6911": {
          "type": "article_2",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image005.jpg",
            "image_size": 0,
            "border_text": "",
            "title": "Step 2:",
            "subtitle": "",
            "text": "<p>Roll out the clay in a suitable thickness. We recommend approximately 0.5 cm/ 1.9 inches.</p>",
            "text2": "",
            "content_width": 450,
            "content_width_image": 450,
            "center": false,
            "fill_height": true,
            "mirror": true,
            "section_background": "",
            "content_background": "",
            "content_text": "",
            "content_accent": "",
            "width": "default",
            "margin": 5,
            "section_padding": 0,
            "padding": 0
          }
        },
        "313c1785-a035-4890-9471-ca37a03c597d11": {
          "type": "article_2",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image006.jpg",
            "image_size": 0,
            "border_text": "",
            "title": "Step 3:",
            "subtitle": "",
            "text": "<p>Press the baby’s foot straight down, and gently press the foot into the clay, to create depth of the footprint.</p><p>It is important that you do this step before doing the final round cutout, as the pressure of the foot can change the outer shape of your final round cutout – making it wonky looking.</p>",
            "text2": "",
            "content_width": 450,
            "content_width_image": 450,
            "center": false,
            "fill_height": true,
            "mirror": false,
            "section_background": "",
            "content_background": "",
            "content_text": "",
            "content_accent": "",
            "width": "default",
            "margin": 5,
            "section_padding": 0,
            "padding": 0
          }
        },
        "ea02ad2d-5d55-4517-837b-45fcf1fe409d1": {
          "type": "article_2",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image007.jpg",
            "image_size": 0,
            "border_text": "",
            "title": "Step 4:",
            "subtitle": "",
            "text": "<p>Take a suitable bowl or big cookie cutter and place it on top of the clay, making sure the foot is in the middle and that there is enough space (at least 2 cm/7.9 inches) from the edge of the foot to the border.</p><p>Now press down the bowl in twisting motions and let the bowl itself cut through the clay.</p><p>Peel away excess clay with your fingers or a regular kitchen knife.</p><p>Pad down the edges with your fingers with a few drops of water, to smooth the edges.</p>",
            "text2": "",
            "content_width": 450,
            "content_width_image": 450,
            "center": false,
            "fill_height": true,
            "mirror": true,
            "section_background": "",
            "content_background": "",
            "content_text": "",
            "content_accent": "",
            "width": "default",
            "margin": 5,
            "section_padding": 0,
            "padding": 0
          }
        },
        "7b4814ad-68d7-48e2-8704-555842f25ebc1": {
          "type": "article_2",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image011.jpg",
            "image_size": 0,
            "border_text": "",
            "title": "Step 5:",
            "subtitle": "",
            "text": "<p>Create the hole approximate 1 cm/3.9 inches from the edge of the border with a straw or a chopstick.</p>",
            "text2": "",
            "content_width": 450,
            "content_width_image": 450,
            "center": false,
            "fill_height": true,
            "mirror": false,
            "section_background": "",
            "content_background": "",
            "content_text": "",
            "content_accent": "",
            "width": "default",
            "margin": 5,
            "section_padding": 0,
            "padding": 0
          }
        },
        "577ef147-1df8-43f0-9b68-74c4521ddfb2": {
          "type": "article_2",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image009.jpg",
            "image_size": 0,
            "border_text": "",
            "title": "Step 6:",
            "subtitle": "",
            "text": "<p>Use your letter stamp to stamp in the name of your baby, while the clay is still wet.</p><p>Let the decoration dry. Read your instructions on the clay pack , for exact drying time.</p>",
            "text2": "",
            "content_width": 450,
            "content_width_image": 450,
            "center": false,
            "fill_height": true,
            "mirror": true,
            "section_background": "",
            "content_background": "",
            "content_text": "",
            "content_accent": "",
            "width": "default",
            "margin": 5,
            "section_padding": 0,
            "padding": 0
          }
        },
        "f2fb43fe-a17a-499a-9f27-e69e943b67ff": {
          "type": "article_2",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image010.jpg",
            "image_size": 0,
            "border_text": "",
            "title": "Step 7:",
            "subtitle": "",
            "text": "<p>Cut a piece of string, in your preferred length, loop it through the hole and tie a knot, so you can hang it. Finally use a marker to write today ’s date or the age of your child on the backside.</p><p><a href=\"/collections/the-first-step\" title=\"Before the first step\"><strong>See collection</strong></a></p>",
            "text2": "",
